WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.475
The Source Register is the
foundation under everything else.

2
00:00:03.475 --> 00:00:08.012
A slide or a video description doesn't
link straight to a publisher's page.

3
00:00:08.012 --> 00:00:12.737
It links to the source's row in this
register, and the row links to the original.

4
00:00:12.737 --> 00:00:16.375
That matters because a released
deck or video can't change,

5
00:00:16.375 --> 00:00:18.800
but publishers move pages all the time.

6
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.788
With the register in between,

7
00:00:20.788 --> 00:00:25.013
a link in a released deck stays
right: only the row has to change.

8
00:00:25.013 --> 00:00:29.687
The register holds 540 sources
today, under three rules.

9
00:00:29.687 --> 00:00:35.488
A source's address is permanent: a row can
be retired, but never deleted or renamed.

10
00:00:35.488 --> 00:00:38.642
Every change goes through
a reviewed pull request,

11
00:00:38.642 --> 00:00:43.450
adds to the revision history, and sends
the page back to its owner for approval.

12
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:47.675
And the weekly source watch reads
every row, shows the result in

13
00:00:47.675 --> 00:00:52.130
the Last scan column, and proposes
fixes, but never edits on its own.
